{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nEvidence + proposal, no code: does a defect pattern from one 2026-08-20 session generalise, and should\nreview grow a criterion? **The question turns out to be already asked, measured and documented in-repo —\nand only partly acted on.** That, not the pattern, is the finding. The first comment holds the instance\ntables, the per-criterion audit, the rejections, and source quotes.\n\n## The pattern (falsifiable)\n\n> **Additive obligation miss.** A change creates a new obligation (contract, invariant, schema field,\n> config key, changed default, new evidence kind, or a second site that must stay in step) and\n> discharges it at some sites that owe it but not all. The missed site is where the defect surfaces.\n\nAll three must be nameable: (1) the obligation; (2) the site(s) that DID discharge it; (3) the site that\ndid NOT. **Falsifier:** if no site ever discharged it, that is a missing guard, not an obligation miss —\nclause (2) is what stops the pattern collapsing into \"a bug is when code is wrong\".\n\n## The prior art that reframes this ticket\n\n`docs/experiments/escaped-bug-review-gap-analysis.md` measured this over **43 bugs closed\n`close_class == regression`**. Its Class 3 (\"CLI ↔ MCP ↔ import-format surface parity\") is exactly this\nquestion and states: **\"No criterion enforces entry-point parity.\"** Its example\n`halfwhite-chordal-stonefly` — a `--class` requirement added to the CLI but not to MCP or NDJSON import\n— survived **9 prior PASS reviews with ZERO findings**.\n\nIt recommended three criteria. **Verified today: `import-integrity` and `ci-gate-compat` appear nowhere\nin `src/` or `.rebar/` — never built.** `surface-parity` was built but narrower: glob-triggered on three\nhardcoded paths rather than content-triggered; **omits the NDJSON/import surface from its own founding\nbug**; and `blocking_enabled: false`. Its subtractive twin `deletion-impact` is content-triggered and\n**blocking@0.60** — same architecture, opposite posture.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Sample A — the 2026-08-20 session: 12 tickets. NOT independent** (one session, one protocol, one\nprompt naming the pattern) — hypothesis-generating only.\n\n**Sample B — INDEPENDENT, two disjoint methods.** *(i)* Random sample of 45 closed bugs (seed 20260820),\nclassifier blind to Sample A → **16 fit**. *(ii)* Targeted hunt: ~200 titles triaged, **41 read in full,\n26 verified, 15 rejected**, spanning **2026-07-08 → 2026-08-19** across unrelated discovery channels.\n**The pattern generalises.** Amplifiers that recur: surface multiplicity; **gate-invisible sites** (two\ninstances missed *external* test modules because they are excluded from the `Verified` gate); guards\ninheriting the omission.\n\n**Copy-propagation is a DIFFERENT mechanism, covered by nothing proposed here.** In\n`conscious-weighable-spittlebug` the missing `cwd=` originates in `57114212cf` (2026-06-12), was copied\nto `9ad46965bd` and `d2dea317ec`, all three fixed in `d575600381` — an omission **deliberately\nimitated**, no contract changed. Here the fix site **is** the cause site with no good→bad transition, a\ncounter-example to \"the fix site is not the cause site\".\n\n## Adversarial analysis\n\n**Base rate, n=45 random:** A=16 (**35.6%**), B=28 (62.2%), C=1; among A, **81% cross-file**.\n**Definition sensitivity is the headline.** Requiring a dated producer commit → **~24%**; loosening to\n\"two things should have stayed in sync\" → **>60%**. The pattern discriminates *only* under the strict\nthree-clause definition. The targeted hunt rejected 15 of 41 — e.g. `kaolinite-head-wildebeest`, a\nperfect-shaped candidate closed **not_a_bug** because the \"missed\" site is test-only.\n\n**Over-fire warning, from the project's own data** (`docs/plan-review-gate.md:263-269`): across\n**18,085** plan-v3 verified findings, the *\"omitted scope site / unenumerated consumer\"* class had\n**1,307** findings, **~90% (1,173) graded `none`**; a blunt widening would have flipped 4.3% of runs\nPASS→BLOCK. Strongest argument **against** a broad criterion, and why the proposal is narrow.\n\n**Selection effects (three).** (1) Sample A is one primed session. (2) Only **65 `caused_by` edges\nacross 704 closed bugs** (<10%) — origin attribution is recorded almost only when `/rebar-debug` traces\nit, so corpus-wide measurement is biased. (3) Both independent samples are *investigated* bugs,\nfavouring the bucket needing three nameable things.\n\n**Sample A cannot indict today's stack.** `surface-parity` shipped **2026-08-19**; every Sample-A origin\ncommit predates it (2026-06-12 → 2026-08-15). Via `registry.glob_triggered_overlays` it glob-fires on\n`9844f6de35`, `0f999860ad`, `d575600381` today and **still** misses all three — its prompt confines\nsiblings to the lib/CLI/MCP triple, while the real missed siblings were `gates.py`, a help `.txt`, and\nthree spawn sites. The case rests on Sample B, not Sample A.\n\n**Actionability: solved.** `deletion-impact`/`surface-parity` already give reviewers repo read tools with\na one-hop sweep — trigger scope and posture, not discoverability, are the constraints.\n**Portability: clean** — criteria are LLM overlays in `.rebar/criteria_routing.json`; no CI involved.\n\n## Does an existing criterion cover it? Partly\n\nAll 49 plan criteria and 14 code-review overlays enumerated; detail in the comment.\n`omits_required_site` is blocking but a **grade**, not a hunter. `T13` runs the right enumeration but\ntriggers only on **prohibitions**, while every instance here is an **addition**. `deletion-impact` is\nthe **subtractive** mirror. `/rebar-debug` Step 7 Axis-2 has the full census but runs **only at debug\ntime**. **Residual gap:** *no criterion asks \"this change adds an obligation — enumerate every surface\nthat owes it and dispose of each.\"*\n\n## Proposal\n\nA broad \"update every consumer\" criterion is **not** warranted (~90% immateriality). By cost-to-value:\n\n- **P0 — close the three documented gap-analysis recommendations, or record why not.** Two never built;\n  the third shipped narrower. Cheapest real progress; no new research needed.\n- **P1 — widen `surface-parity` to what was recommended:** content-triggered, channel list extended to\n  the NDJSON/import surface, plus a calibration run to decide blocking on `deletion-impact`'s precedent.\n- **P2 — widen `T13`'s trigger lexicon from *prohibition* to *obligation*.** A prompt edit.\n- **P3 (only if residue remains) — project overlay `project.obligation-parity`**, the additive mirror of\n  `deletion-impact`, importing Step 7 Axis-2's census; triage MIGRATED/EXEMPTED/**UNCOVERED**; abstain\n  when the obligation is not reducible to a checkable pattern. Anti-fire threshold mirroring\n  `project.portability`: a finding needs (a) the cited added line, (b) `path:line` of a site that DID\n  discharge it in the same diff, (c) `path:line` of one that did NOT, (d) the observable consequence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A ruling on P0-P3 — adopt / adopt-narrowed / reject — with reasons.\n- [ ] `import-integrity` / `ci-gate-compat`: built, or the decision not to written into\n      `docs/experiments/escaped-bug-review-gap-analysis.md` so it stops reading as three open recs.\n- [ ] Any criterion promoted to blocking has a calibration replay vs `deletion-impact`'s precedent and\n      the ~90%-`none` omitted-scope-site rate.\n- [ ] Any adopted prompt encodes all four evidence elements (a)-(d); one lacking any is rejected.\n- [ ] Replayed against >=5 origin commits named here (`9844f6de35`, `0f999860ad`, `27b868ba55`,\n      `746c1ba2e9`, `f943c7ef58`), hit/miss per commit; catching none ⇒ not worth shipping.\n- [ ] FP exposure measured on recent PASSes, recorded in `docs/code-review-fp-ledger.md`.\n- [ ] No CI provider required to trigger it (`project.portability` clean).\n- [ ] If all rejected, reasons land beside the plan-v3 field-evidence paragraph in\n      `docs/plan-review-gate.md`. (Out of scope throughout: the copy-propagation variant.)\n\n## Verification\n\nAnalysis-only: the ruling, plus (if adopted) the replay and FP-ledger entry."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787273642272398001,"uuid":"a16049b9-6ae2-4f5f-9dd6-c8644a549198"}